#: ../../source/simulation.rst:2
msgid "Simulation, URDF, SDFormat and MJCF"
msgstr "Simulación, URDF, SDFormat y MJCF"

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:4
msgid ""
"PartCAD can read a `URDF <https://wiki.ros.org/urdf>`_ file as an "
"assembly (``type: urdf``), write one back out (``pc export -t urdf``), "
"and convert an assembly between URDF and ASSY in either direction (``pc "
"convert assembly``). URDF is the one of these three PartCAD implements "
"itself, because it describes a robot rather than any one engine's world "
"and ROS, MuJoCo, PyBullet and Isaac all read it."
msgstr ""
"PartCAD puede leer un archivo `URDF <https://wiki.ros.org/urdf>`_ como un"
" ensamblaje (``type: urdf``), volver a escribir uno (``pc export -t "
"urdf``), y convertir un ensamblaje entre URDF y ASSY en ambas direcciones"
" (``pc convert assembly``). URDF es el único de estos tres que implementa"
" el propio PartCAD, porque describe un robot y no el mundo de un motor "
"concreto, y ROS, MuJoCo, PyBullet e Isaac lo leen todos."

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:11
msgid ""
"The same machinery reads and writes `SDFormat <http://sdformat.org/>`_ --"
" what Gazebo describes a simulation *world* in -- against a :ref:`scene "
"<scenes>` rather than an assembly, and `MJCF "
"<https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html>`_, what "
"`MuJoCo <https://mujoco.org/>`_ describes a model in, as either. Neither "
"is in this wheel: each is declared by the plugin package for its engine "
"and named through it (``sim-gazebo:world``, ``sim-mujoco:mjcf``). See `An"
" engine's own scene format is its plugin's`_ below."
msgstr ""
"La misma maquinaria lee y escribe `SDFormat <http://sdformat.org/>`_ -- "
"aquello en lo que Gazebo describe un *mundo* de simulación -- contra una "
":ref:`escena <scenes>` en lugar de un ensamblaje, y `MJCF "
"<https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html>`_, aquello en"
" lo que `MuJoCo <https://mujoco.org/>`_ describe un modelo, como "
"cualquiera de los dos. Ninguno de los dos está en este wheel: cada uno lo"
" declara el paquete de plugin de su motor y se nombra a través de él "
"(``sim-gazebo:world``, ``sim-mujoco:mjcf``). Consulte `An engine's own "
"scene format is its plugin's`_ más abajo."

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:20
msgid ""
"It can also **run** one. ``simulate:`` is where a part or an assembly "
"says what it is supposed to do -- or not do -- once it is placed in a "
"world and the world is switched on, and ``pc sim`` places it, runs it and"
" checks the claim. This page is the design record for all of that: what "
"the conversions actually preserve, what they cannot, and what it would "
"take for PartCAD to hold everything a physical simulation needs."
msgstr ""
"También puede **ejecutar** una. ``simulate:`` es donde una pieza o un "
"ensamblaje dicen qué se supone que deben hacer -- o no hacer -- una vez "
"colocados en un mundo y encendido ese mundo, y ``pc sim`` lo coloca, lo "
"ejecuta y comprueba la afirmación. Esta página es el registro de diseño "
"de todo eso: qué preservan realmente las conversiones, qué no pueden "
"preservar, y qué haría falta para que PartCAD contuviera todo lo que "
"necesita una simulación física."

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:27
msgid ""
"The \"What exists today\" section describes what is built. Everything "
"after it is a proposal, and none of it is implemented."
msgstr ""
"La sección \"What exists today\" describe lo que está construido. Todo lo"
" que viene después es una propuesta, y nada de ello está implementado."

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:36
msgid "What exists today"
msgstr "Lo que existe hoy"

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:39
msgid "Reading a URDF"
msgstr "Leer un URDF"

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:41
msgid ""
"A URDF reaches a package by the same two commands any other foreign file "
"does, and they mean the same two things they mean for a STEP file. ``pc "
"add assembly urdf <path>`` *declares* it: the package points at the file,"
" the file stays a URDF, and its links become parts as it is read. ``pc "
"import assembly <path>`` *converts* it: the package gains an ``stl`` part"
" per link, an interface pair per joint and an ``.assy``, and nothing "
"points at the URDF afterwards. The import is the conversion described in "
"`Converting between the two`_, run against a declaration that lives only "
"for the length of it - which is what lets the source file sit anywhere, "
"the way a STEP file being imported does."
msgstr ""
"Un URDF llega a un paquete por los mismos dos comandos que cualquier otro"
" archivo ajeno, y significan las mismas dos cosas que significan para un "
"archivo STEP. ``pc add assembly urdf <path>`` lo *declara*: el paquete "
"apunta al archivo, el archivo sigue siendo un URDF, y sus enlaces se "
"convierten en piezas a medida que se lee. ``pc import assembly <path>`` "
"lo *convierte*: el paquete gana una pieza ``stl`` por enlace, un par de "
"interfaces por articulación y un ``.assy``, y después nada apunta al "
"URDF. La importación es la conversión descrita en `Converting between the"
" two`_, ejecutada contra una declaración que vive solo lo que dura -- que"
" es lo que permite que el archivo de origen esté en cualquier sitio, "
"igual que ocurre con un archivo STEP que se importa."

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:51
msgid ""
"``AssemblyFactoryUrdf`` drives ``wrapper_import_urdf`` in a python "
"sandbox. The sandbox parses the file with ROS's own ``urdf_parser_py``, "
"walks the joint tree from the root link with every joint at its zero "
"position, resolves each link's geometry, and hands back plain data. The "
"core registers one part per shape - ``<assembly>/<link>`` for a link that"
" is one, and ``<assembly>/<link>/<n>`` under a sub-assembly for a link "
"that is several - and builds the very same ``Assembly``/``AssemblyChild``"
" tree an ASSY file produces."
msgstr ""
"``AssemblyFactoryUrdf`` controla ``wrapper_import_urdf`` en un sandbox de"
" Python. El sandbox analiza el archivo con el propio ``urdf_parser_py`` "
"de ROS, recorre el árbol de articulaciones desde el enlace raíz con todas"
" las articulaciones en su posición cero, resuelve la geometría de cada "
"enlace, y devuelve datos simples. El núcleo registra una pieza por forma "
"-- ``<assembly>/<link>`` para un enlace que es una sola, y "
"``<assembly>/<link>/<n>`` bajo un subensamblaje para un enlace que son "
"varias -- y construye exactamente el mismo árbol "
"``Assembly``/``AssemblyChild`` que produce un archivo ASSY."

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:59
msgid ""
"The links go into **one flat list**, each at its absolute placement. The "
"joint tree is the robot's kinematics; an assembly is one static "
"configuration of it, so nesting a sub-assembly per joint would make an "
"arm as deep as it has joints and say nothing the placement does not. The "
"relative placements are recorded in a link table instead, which is what "
"the ASSY conversion turns into joints."
msgstr ""
"Los enlaces van a **una lista plana**, cada uno en su colocación "
"absoluta. El árbol de articulaciones es la cinemática del robot; un "
"ensamblaje es una configuración estática de ella, así que anidar un "
"subensamblaje por articulación haría que un brazo fuera tan profundo como"
" articulaciones tiene y no diría nada que la colocación no diga. Las "
"colocaciones relativas se registran en su lugar en una tabla de enlaces, "
"que es lo que la conversión a ASSY convierte en articulaciones."

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:65
msgid ""
"Nothing is rewritten that does not have to be: a ``<mesh>`` becomes a "
"part that reads the very file the URDF named, and the ``<origin>`` that "
"places it becomes a location rather than a transform baked into a copy of"
" the geometry. Only ``<box>``/``<cylinder>``/``<sphere>`` are generated, "
"because there is no file to point at."
msgstr ""
"No se reescribe nada que no haya que reescribir: una ``<mesh>`` se "
"convierte en una pieza que lee el mismísimo archivo que nombró el URDF, y"
" el ``<origin>`` que la coloca se convierte en una ubicación y no en una "
"transformación horneada en una copia de la geometría. Solo se generan "
"``<box>``/``<cylinder>``/``<sphere>``, porque no hay ningún archivo al "
"que apuntar."

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:71
msgid ""
"A link is built from its **collision** geometry when it states both, "
"since that is the shape a simulator resolves contact against; "
"``ignoreCollision`` reverses that per link or wholesale. The geometry "
"that was not used is not discarded: it becomes the part "
"``<assembly>/<link>/<visual|collision>``, defined and exportable but not "
"placed in the assembly."
msgstr ""
"Un enlace se construye a partir de su geometría de **colisión** cuando "
"indica ambas, ya que esa es la forma contra la que un simulador resuelve "
"el contacto; ``ignoreCollision`` lo invierte por enlace o en bloque. La "
"geometría que no se usó no se descarta: se convierte en la pieza "
"``<assembly>/<link>/<visual|collision>``, definida y exportable pero no "
"colocada en el ensamblaje."

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:77
msgid ""
"What the link says about its physics is **copied field by field into "
"named PartCAD properties**, in PartCAD's own units. ``<inertial>`` "
"becomes ``mass``, ``centerOfMass`` and ``inertia``; the friction and "
"contact settings of a ``<gazebo>`` block become ``friction``, "
"``contactStiffness`` and the rest; ``<material>`` becomes ``material`` "
"and ``color``. A joint's ``<limit>``, ``<dynamics>``, "
"``<safety_controller>`` and ``<mimic>`` become the ``motion`` and "
"``physics`` sections of the interface it turns into. Nothing is nested "
"under the name of the format it came from, and nothing is opaque."
msgstr ""
"Lo que el enlace dice sobre su física se **copia campo a campo a "
"propiedades de PartCAD con nombre**, en las unidades propias de PartCAD. "
"``<inertial>`` se convierte en ``mass``, ``centerOfMass`` e ``inertia``; "
"los ajustes de fricción y contacto de un bloque ``<gazebo>`` se "
"convierten en ``friction``, ``contactStiffness`` y los demás; "
"``<material>`` se convierte en ``material`` y ``color``. El ``<limit>``, "
"el ``<dynamics>``, el ``<safety_controller>`` y el ``<mimic>`` de una "
"articulación se convierten en las secciones ``motion`` y ``physics`` de "
"la interfaz en la que se convierte. Nada se anida bajo el nombre del "
"formato del que provino, y nada es opaco."

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:86
msgid ""
"That choice has a cost and it is deliberate: URDF that no property covers"
" stops the import, naming what it found. Core URDF is a closed "
"vocabulary, so an unknown element there means PartCAD is out of date and "
"the remedy is to extend the tables in ``wrapper_import_urdf.py``. "
"``<gazebo>`` is an open extension point, so an unknown setting there is "
"reported rather than fatal unless the assembly asks for ``strict: true``."
" The export mirrors it: a PartCAD property URDF cannot state is reported "
"at info level rather than dropped in silence."
msgstr ""
"Esa elección tiene un coste y es deliberado: el URDF que ninguna "
"propiedad cubre detiene la importación, nombrando lo que encontró. El "
"URDF básico es un vocabulario cerrado, así que un elemento desconocido "
"ahí significa que PartCAD está desactualizado y el remedio es ampliar las"
" tablas de ``wrapper_import_urdf.py``. ``<gazebo>`` es un punto de "
"extensión abierto, así que un ajuste desconocido ahí se informa en lugar "
"de ser fatal, salvo que el ensamblaje pida ``strict: true``. La "
"exportación lo refleja: de una propiedad de PartCAD que URDF no puede "
"expresar se informa a nivel info en lugar de descartarse en silencio."

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:94
msgid ""
"Nor does anything record the link's name or its parent. The part *is* "
"named after the link, and the joint tree is the URDF file - which is "
"still on disk and is read afresh - or, once converted, the ``connect:`` "
"sections of the ASSY. A second copy in a properties section would only be"
" a second thing to keep right."
msgstr ""
"Tampoco hay nada que registre el nombre del enlace ni el de su padre. La "
"pieza *lleva* el nombre del enlace, y el árbol de articulaciones es el "
"archivo URDF -- que sigue en disco y se lee de nuevo -- o, una vez "
"convertido, las secciones ``connect:`` del ASSY. Una segunda copia en una"
" sección de propiedades sería solo una segunda cosa que mantener "
"correcta."

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:100
msgid "Writing a URDF"
msgstr "Escribir un URDF"

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:102
msgid ""
"The URDF exporter (``//builtin/export``'s ``export_urdf.py``) is handed "
"the assembly *tree* rather than the compound it decodes to - which is "
"what ``decode: false`` on its declaration asks for. Each node becomes a "
"link, each parent/child relation a fixed joint carrying that child's "
"placement, and each node with geometry gets an STL written next to the "
"URDF. A shape that appears more than once is written once and referenced "
"by every link that uses it."
msgstr ""
"Al exportador de URDF (el ``export_urdf.py`` de ``//builtin/export``) se "
"le entrega el *árbol* del ensamblaje en lugar del compuesto al que se "
"decodifica -- que es lo que pide el ``decode: false`` de su declaración. "
"Cada nodo se convierte en un enlace, cada relación padre/hijo en una "
"articulación fija que lleva la colocación de ese hijo, y cada nodo con "
"geometría obtiene un STL escrito junto al URDF. Una forma que aparece más"
" de una vez se escribe una sola vez y la referencian todos los enlaces "
"que la usan."

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:109
msgid ""
"A sub-assembly whose children are named *under* it - ``wrist`` holding "
"``wrist/1`` and ``wrist/2`` - goes back out as one link with a "
"``<visual>`` per shape, at the offset each was placed at, rather than as "
"a frame link with a link per shape. So a link of several visuals survives"
" the round trip as itself. The slash is the whole of the rule, and it "
"needs nothing recorded anywhere: it is the same convention the import "
"uses to name those parts in the first place."
msgstr ""
"Un subensamblaje cuyos hijos se nombran *bajo* él -- ``wrist`` "
"conteniendo ``wrist/1`` y ``wrist/2`` -- sale de vuelta como un solo "
"enlace con un ``<visual>`` por forma, en el desplazamiento en el que se "
"colocó cada una, en lugar de como un enlace de referencia con un enlace "
"por forma. Así que un enlace de varios visuales sobrevive al viaje de ida"
" y vuelta siendo él mismo. La barra es toda la regla, y no necesita que "
"se registre nada en ninguna parte: es la misma convención que usa la "
"importación para nombrar esas piezas desde el principio."

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:116
msgid ""
"The joint *tree* does not survive: the export mirrors the assembly, and a"
" URDF assembly is flat, so what comes out is a root frame with every link"
" fixed to it directly. That is an honest reading - the exported joints "
"are all fixed because PartCAD holds one static configuration, and a star "
"of fixed joints is what that is. The chain is preserved where it means "
"something, in ``pc convert assembly -t assy``, and a faithful re-export "
"would read it back from there rather than from anything stashed on the "
"parts."
msgstr ""
"El *árbol* de articulaciones no sobrevive: la exportación refleja el "
"ensamblaje, y un ensamblaje URDF es plano, así que lo que sale es un "
"sistema de referencia raíz con todos los enlaces fijados directamente a "
"él. Esa es una lectura honesta -- las articulaciones exportadas son todas"
" fijas porque PartCAD contiene una configuración estática, y una estrella"
" de articulaciones fijas es lo que eso es. La cadena se preserva donde "
"significa algo, en ``pc convert assembly -t assy``, y una reexportación "
"fiel la volvería a leer de ahí y no de nada guardado en las piezas."

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:124
msgid ""
"What a part states about itself is written into the URDF element that "
"states it: mass, centre of mass and inertia into ``<inertial>``, friction"
" and the contact parameters into a ``<gazebo>`` block, "
"``material``/``color`` into ``<material>``. A part that states none of "
"its mass properties is written no differently, because PartCAD has "
"already worked them out: OCCT measured the solid's volume, its centroid "
"and its inertia at unit density as the part was built, and the density of"
" what the part is made of turns those into a mass, a centre of mass and "
"an inertia (``partcad.physics``). They reach the exporter in the part's "
"properties, under the names a part would state them under, and the "
"exporter writes them - this one, and the MJCF and SDFormat ones the "
"simulation plugins carry, all the same way, because none of them works a "
"mass out. Every value is resolved in one order:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:137
msgid "what the part states, as stated;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:138
msgid "its ``density`` - one it states itself, or else its material's;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:139
msgid ""
"for an export only, the ``density`` parameter of the export, else 2700 "
"kg/m³ (aluminium), for a part that states no density and is made of "
"nothing that does."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:143
msgid ""
"A part that states its mass and not its inertia gets its solid's inertia "
"scaled to that mass, so it turns the way its shape says at the weight it "
"says. The centre of mass and the inertia come from the same density as "
"the mass, so the three cannot disagree. ``pc info`` reports the same "
"values as ``MassProperties``, each with where it came from, so what it "
"says a part weighs is what a simulation of it weighs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:150
msgid ""
"What an exporter still does is add up a link made of several shapes - "
"``wrist/1`` in aluminium, ``wrist/2`` in steel - each placed where the "
"link holds it, its inertia turned with it and moved to the common centre "
"of mass, so that the link balances where the steel pulls it. That "
"arithmetic is ``mass_properties`` in PartCAD's ``wrappers/`` directory, "
"beside ``urdf_common``, and it is the one copy of it: the plugins import "
"it the way they import ``urdf_common``, and carry none of their own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:158
msgid ""
"Every density is in kg/m³ - a material's, a part's and an export's - so "
"none is ever converted on the way, and there is no factor of a million "
"anywhere to get wrong."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:162
msgid ""
"A link's name, and the properties written under it, come from the shape "
"the exporter is handed, and both travel on that shape together. This used"
" to be the one place the shape cache showed through: the cache is keyed "
"by geometry, deliberately, so that two parts reading the same mesh file "
"do not compute it twice, and the entry used to carry the name of "
"whichever part wrote it - so the other part read back wearing a name that"
" was not its own, and the properties looked up under that name were the "
"wrong part's or nobody's. The entry no longer stores that outer layer at "
"all. What identifies the shape being asked for - its name, its label, its"
" placement, and what it reports about itself - is stamped onto the "
"payload from the asking object's own configuration every time an entry is"
" read, so parts that share geometry each get themselves back."
msgstr ""
"El nombre de un enlace, y las propiedades escritas bajo él, provienen de "
"la forma que se le entrega al exportador, y ambos viajan juntos en esa "
"forma. Este solía ser el único sitio donde la caché de formas se "
"transparentaba: la caché se indexa por geometría, deliberadamente, para "
"que dos piezas que leen el mismo archivo de malla no la calculen dos "
"veces, y la entrada llevaba el nombre de la pieza que la hubiera escrito "
"-- así que la otra pieza volvía llevando un nombre que no era el suyo, y "
"las propiedades buscadas bajo ese nombre eran las de la pieza equivocada "
"o las de nadie. La entrada ya no almacena en absoluto esa capa exterior. "
"Lo que identifica la forma que se pide -- su nombre, su etiqueta, su "
"colocación y lo que informa sobre sí misma -- se estampa en la carga útil"
" a partir de la configuración propia del objeto que pregunta cada vez que"
" se lee una entrada, de modo que las piezas que comparten geometría se "
"recuperan cada una a sí misma."

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:174
msgid ""
"The stamp reaches the shape that was asked for and no further. Inside a "
"cached assembly the children sit in the entry with the names, labels and "
"properties they were built with, because down there they are not who is "
"asking - they are what the tree is made of, as much a part of the answer "
"as the geometry. So a link exported from a part is that part; a link "
"exported from a child of a cached assembly is whatever that child was "
"when the tree was cached, and it takes a change the assembly actually "
"hashes, or ``pc system reset``, to build it again."
msgstr ""
"El estampado llega a la forma que se pidió y no más allá. Dentro de un "
"ensamblaje en caché, los hijos están en la entrada con los nombres, las "
"etiquetas y las propiedades con los que se construyeron, porque ahí abajo"
" no son quienes preguntan -- son de lo que está hecho el árbol, tan parte"
" de la respuesta como la geometría. Así que un enlace exportado de una "
"pieza es esa pieza; un enlace exportado de un hijo de un ensamblaje en "
"caché es lo que fuera ese hijo cuando se guardó el árbol en caché, y hace"
" falta un cambio en algo que el ensamblaje realmente incluya en su hash, "
"o ``pc system reset``, para volver a construirlo."

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:182
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"What a shape reports about itself is cached too, in an entry of its own "
"beside the geometry - the geometry's key with ``-props`` appended. Both "
"are filled by the one run that actually instantiates the shape, and they "
"are read apart: a consumer after a part's material need not pull its BREP"
" back out of the cache, and a cache written before that entry existed is "
"a miss for the properties and not for the geometry. It is not what the "
"stamp above is made of, though: that entry is keyed on the geometry, so "
"what sits in it belongs to the geometry. What the object asking reports "
"is its own ``properties:`` section, and only that."
msgstr ""
"Lo que una forma informa sobre sí misma también se guarda en caché, en "
"una entrada propia junto a la geometría -- la clave de la geometría con "
"``-props`` añadido. Ambas las rellena la única ejecución que realmente "
"instancia la forma, y se leen por separado: un consumidor que busca el "
"material de una pieza no necesita sacar su BREP de la caché, y una caché "
"escrita antes de que existiera esa entrada es un fallo para las "
"propiedades y no para la geometría. No es, sin embargo, de lo que está "
"hecho el estampado anterior: esa entrada se indexa por la geometría, así "
"que lo que hay en ella pertenece a la geometría -- que es donde "
"aterrizaría una propiedad *derivada* (el punto 2 más abajo). Lo que "
"informa el objeto que pregunta es su propia sección ``properties:``, y "
"solo eso."

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:191
msgid ""
"A *derived* property is not cached there either, and the reason is the "
"same key. A mass is the solid times a density, and the density lives in a"
" ``materials:`` section or a ``properties:`` one, neither of which the "
"geometry's hash covers - so a mass cached beside the geometry would "
"outlive an edit to the density it was worked out from. It has an entry of"
" its own instead (``partcad.physics``), holding the part's volume, mass, "
"centre of mass and inertia, under a key made of the part's own cache key "
"- which every edit to the CAD moves - and of everything the derivation "
"reads that the part's key does not cover: the density it was weighed at "
"and where that came from (a stated density, the material that lent it, or"
" an export's fallback), and every value the part states that a derived "
"one would otherwise fill in. An edit to a material's density or to a "
"stated mass is therefore a new entry as well, and an edit to anything "
"that does not weigh - a material's description, a part's friction - is "
"not. ``pc info``, an export and the IDE read the same entry, and a hit "
"answers without the geometry. A miss works the values out from what the "
"geometry's own entry carries: the volume, and the centroid and inertia at"
" unit density OCCT measures as the shape is built."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:210
msgid "Converting between the two"
msgstr "Convertir entre los dos"

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:212
msgid ""
"``pc convert assembly`` rewrites the package rather than just producing a"
" file. To URDF it writes the ``.urdf`` and its meshes and switches the "
"declaration over. To ASSY it writes an ``stl`` part for every link, an "
"interface pair for every joint, and an ``.assy`` whose nodes use "
"``connect:`` - so the result is an assembly stated the way PartCAD states"
" one, not a transcription of coordinates. How the joints become "
"interfaces is `URDF joints as PartCAD interfaces`_ below."
msgstr ""
"``pc convert assembly`` reescribe el paquete en lugar de limitarse a "
"producir un archivo. A URDF escribe el ``.urdf`` y sus mallas y cambia la"
" declaración. A ASSY escribe una pieza ``stl`` por cada enlace, un par de"
" interfaces por cada articulación, y un ``.assy`` cuyos nodos usan "
"``connect:`` -- de modo que el resultado es un ensamblaje expresado como "
"PartCAD expresa uno, no una transcripción de coordenadas. Cómo se "
"convierten las articulaciones en interfaces está en `URDF joints as "
"PartCAD interfaces`_ más abajo."

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:220
msgid "What the round trip preserves"
msgstr "Qué preserva el viaje de ida y vuelta"

#: ../../source/simulation.rst:222
msgid ""
"``examples/produce_assembly_assy:logo`` exported to URDF and read back as"
" a ``urdf`` assembly puts every shape back where it was, under the name "
"it had, built from the same geometry - flattened, because a URDF has no "
"way to say \"these parts belong together\" other than by joining them. "
"That is the whole of what survives."
msgstr ""
"``examples/produce_assembly_assy:logo`` exportado a URDF y leído de nuevo"
" como un ensamblaje ``urdf`` vuelve a poner cada forma donde estaba, con "
"el nombre que tenía, construida a partir de la misma geometría -- "
"aplanado, porque un URDF no tiene forma de decir \"estas piezas van "
"juntas\" salvo uniéndolas. Eso es todo lo que sobrevive."

